> It doesn't cover ad-hoc unionsYes and no. C# unions aren’t sealed types, that’s a separate feature. But they are strictly nominal - they must be formally declared:    union Foo(Bar, Baz);

Which isn’t at all the same as saying:    Bar | Baz

It is the same as the night and day difference between tuples and nominal records.

